# db-backup schedule (supercronic; TZ from the container's TZ env).
#
# Twice-daily backups → ≤12h loss window (approved §12.4), 12h apart, both off
# the drill window. Weekly restore-drill Sunday 04:00, deliberately clear of the
# 02:00/14:00 backups so the scratch restore never contends with a live dump
# (approved §12.3: off-peak, no overlap).
#
# The WEEKLY restore-drill decrypts with the machine key (AGE_IDENTITY, held as
# an operational copy in ACM) so restorability is proven continuously. The
# QUARTERLY manual drill is human-run (NOT cron) and must instead mount the
# off-server private key via AGE_IDENTITY_FILE, leaving AGE_IDENTITY unset, so the
# cold-custody recovery path stays exercised. See README "age identity & drills".
#
# min hour dom mon dow  command
  0   2    *   *   *    /app/backup.sh
  0   14   *   *   *    /app/backup.sh
  0   4    *   *   0    /app/restore-drill.sh
